  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indigenous families in Chiapas furtherjng sustainable smallholder agriculture and a culture of peace.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This amendment provides Xilotl with three additional years and $ 286,935 to strengthen its sustainable agriculture and entrepreneurship activities, while simultaneously expanding its efforts to address violence against women through its network of men and women promoters. Xilotlt will implement evidence-based programs in four communities to promote positive parenting and build social cohesion while reducing gender-based and generational violence. As part of the amendment, Xilolt is mobilizing an additional $ 620,405 in counterpart funding to the grant agreement. This grant advances the IAF?s strategic initiative to support community-led efforts to mitigate and prevent chronic violence.</narrative>
  </description>
